# Source of truth for the MicroGui PACKAGE version.
#
# The $(GitVersion) macro in package.xml is resolved by the OpenTAP SDK
# ("tap sdk gitversion") from the base "version" below plus the git history:
#
#   * A commit on the default (beta) branch that is NOT tagged gets a
#     "-beta.N" prerelease, where N counts commits since the last change to
#     "version".
#   * A commit carrying an annotated tag (v<major>.<minor>.<patch>) gets a
#     clean release with no prerelease suffix.
#
# The 8-char commit hash is always appended as build metadata (+<hash>).
#
# Example — the same commit, before and after tagging:
#
#   untagged:  MicroGui.0.0.3-beta.4+b4d59198.TapPackage
#   tagged:    git tag -a v0.0.3   ->   MicroGui.0.0.3+b4d59198.TapPackage
#
# So to ship a release, tag the commit; the "-beta.N" part disappears.
#
# NOTE: the value must be on the SAME line as "version =" (the parser reads
# "key = value" per line). Keep the base value in sync with the <Version>
# property in MicroGui.csproj (which drives the title bar when running from
# the build output).
version = 0.0.3

# Commits from this branch are treated as prereleases ("-beta.N").
beta branch = main

# A commit is a clean release when it carries an annotated tag matching the
# SDK default pattern (v<major>.<minor>.<patch>), so no "release tag" override
# is needed.
